WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:06.250
What a remarkable moment... The Ten Stonehearts have welcomed their youngest-ever P46.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.700
Aventurine, congratulations on making it into the deep end of the IPC~

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.641
Although... wasn't the last P46 the one you personally took out, Opal?

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.350
Though, "Aventurine" is synonymous with surprises, no?

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.350
Thank you for your kind words...

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:32.150
May we all live up to Diamond's trust in the journey ahead.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:38.675
First the wiretaps, now the impeachment...

00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:42.550
Couldn't wait to roll out the welcome wagon, huh?

00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:47.500
Jade was right...

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.775
Better have "friends" if you wanna secure a foothold here.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.975
Now then... where should I start looking for you (traitor)?

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:09.400
Oswaldo's schedule is mapped down to the minute he brushes his teeth.

00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:13.466
Muddlefudge, what're ya lookin' to trade?

00:01:13.466 --> 00:01:16.950
Keep tabs on him. The longer, the better.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.900
Our thanks to the Ten Stonehearts for their support during the battle against Irontomb.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.500
Thanks for providing us with the gravitational wave data.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.075
May we continue to support one another.

00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:33.325
Supplies received.

00:01:33.475 --> 00:01:36.150
Celenova's Legion has been biding its time of late.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.441
No matter. Just keep me posted if anything comes up.

00:01:41.525 --> 00:01:44.925
Mr. Zazzad (Head of the Talent Motivation Department), thank you for providing Agate's files.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.275
You'll have my support at the next cross-department meeting.

00:01:51.925 --> 00:01:57.100
Thanks to your generous funding, the Knights are one step closer to the Beauty!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.633
Don't mention it.

00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:01.066
But could I ask you to investigate something for me?

00:02:01.066 --> 00:02:02.400
What exactly did Opal destroy...

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.600
on this planet?

00:02:09.525 --> 00:02:11.575
The chips are in the pot...

00:02:13.225 --> 00:02:16.750
Now... which card will seal the win?

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.250
Oh? Time to cash in.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.825
I've analyzed this dataset based on your markers.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.641
What trick are you pulling this time, Gambler?

00:02:32.766 --> 00:02:34.966
With every Lord Ravager at the Irontomb battle,

00:02:34.966 --> 00:02:37.900
Archforger finally left a trail.

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:43.425
Come on, let's see if this absurd theory of mine holds up.

00:02:44.775 --> 00:02:48.008
Hmph. Pulling data from the Deep Web?

00:02:48.183 --> 00:02:49.500
You mean business.

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.475
Now, let the game of cat and mouse begin.

00:02:59.475 --> 00:03:01.808
Search initiated, matching sequence started...

00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:04.375
The Legion: No results.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.950
Architects: No results.

00:03:05.125 --> 00:03:07.475
Nomadic Miners: No results.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.233
Marketing Development Department: No results.

00:03:08.233 --> 00:03:09.450
Do you wish to continue?

00:03:10.575 --> 00:03:13.175
There's still a blind spot.

00:03:19.525 --> 00:03:21.700
Warning! Warning!

00:03:22.475 --> 00:03:25.800
Match Rate: 99.93%.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.633
The Ten Stonehearts' traitor is the Lord Ravager (Archforger)

00:03:34.633 --> 00:03:37.800
aiming for the Preservation?

00:03:42.575 --> 00:03:44.575
Looks like the wind's picking up.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.950
Astropolis caught in the storm...

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.300
Who will have the last laugh?

